      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Don't touch stay away. To be honest I've been burnt by Solarhart Dubbo. I've also been burnt by a local electrician. In saying that I know nothing about electricity. I hate the stuff. Can't see it can't smell it and by the time you know it's there its too late. So I am happy to pay somebody else to deal with it. I dont quibble I don't haggle just tell me what it costs and make it so. I'm quite up front about that. I trust that they will do the right thing as professionals. However, I can pick b.s. I have been b.s'. to by both sides and I'm not happy. Currently (excuse the pun) I have invested $15600 in local Dubbo businesses to install solar. Currently I have no current as the 3 phase wires need to complete the circuit are sitting rolled up in my switch board and at my shed...why because my electrician says it's Solarhart job to join them to the breakers and Solarhart says the electrician has ripped me off as that is his job. In fairness to myself when the issue was pointed out to me I referred to my default setting for electricity...tell me what it will cost and make it so. Ok so after multiple conversations and promises that Solarhart Dubbos will attend to making the system work or I will be called back....nothing. The system is installed but can't operate. Nobody rings back and what really stings is that as i did it via interest free so Solarhart was paid in full BEFORE they did they work.....so I have no leverage to get the job finished....the job they knew needed to be done from the get go....I even asked them to quote me for their electrician  to do the work but nup...we will send you his number...still waiting ....Don't get me wrong the guys who did the roof work are good guys and id personally rank them high but i have been bs'd to by the guys on the ground and im not impressed so my advice to you is....buying local is not always the best outcome...",
